      <transcript>BARAГALXA-</transcript>
      <definition>[= baralxa-] v, 1. To look up, glance upward; to have an interview or an audience with a dignitary; to present oneself -to ( with dat.-lIoc. preceding).</definition>
      <page>83</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠪᠠᠷᠠᠭᠠᠯᠬᠠᠬᠣᠢ ᠎ᠶᠢ ᠠᠶᠢᠯᠠᠳᠬᠠᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>--xui ji ailadxaxu</transcript>
          <definition>To request an audience.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠪᠠᠷᠠᠭᠠᠯᠬᠠᠬᠣᠢ ᠢ ᠰᠣᠶᠤᠷᠬᠠᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>--xui i sojurxaxu</transcript>
          <definition>To grant an audience</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠨᠣᠶᠠᠨ ᠎ᠳᠤ ᠪᠠᠷᠠᠭᠠᠯᠬᠠᠬᠣ</unicode>
          <transcript>nojan du --xu</transcript>
          <definition>To have an audience with a nojan (q. v.).</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
